# Guest disks and helper disks. Multi-gigabyte and re-derivable; the hashes that
# stand in for them are recorded in the host repo's plan/0002 and plan/0003.
*.raw
*.img
rollback/
work/

# Captured guest frames. Screenshots are evidence for a run, not source.
*.ppm
*.png

# Dumped guest memory and firmware images. The ROM dumps are AMD firmware: the
# hashes recorded in plan/0003 stand in for them and the card re-dumps on demand.
*.bin
*.rom

# Serial and monitor logs from a run, including a probe's own stdout.
*.log
*.out

# OVMF variable stores. Copied fresh per run; nothing persists between boots.
*.fd

# Editor and tool backups.
*.bak

# Build outputs. The CSMWrap image is built from the Where-room component's pinned
# source in its own toolchain and deployed to the guest's FAT16 partition; the copy
# that used to sit here was an untracked build that no longer matched any pin.
*.efi

# Superseded by the fix as committed in the CSMWrap fork at 8381c59. A second copy of
# the same patch would drift from the commit that actually carries it.
csmwrap-e820-nvs-gap.patch

# Third-party binaries vendored for a one-off inspection. amdvbflash is the only
# one, it was used once to read the card's ROM, and it is not part of the rig.
tools/

# A stray file named "-r" appeared here once: a `sed -r` that took the flag as the
# script argument wrote the card ROM to a file called "-r". .gitignore patterns do not
# match a name that starts with a dash, so it showed as untracked instead of ignored.
-r
